    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">RSSH/PP LAB-2 Percentage of molecular diagnostic analyzers achieving at least 85% functionality (ability to test samples) during the reporting period</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">This indicator is cumulative. Based on the NPHL POC GeneXpert performance review report for January &#x2013;December 2022, there are 32 facilities that have POC technology, and these constitute the denominator. The denominator however will keep changing based on the planned deployment and expansion of POC Genexpart platforms. Currently only JTH has utilisation rate of at least 85%. For July &#x2013;Dec 2023 semester all facilities with utilisation rates above 60% are expected to reach at least 85%. These are Yambio State Hosp (64%), Yirol (67%) and Aweil (60%). For Jan-June 2024, an additional 5 facilities with current utilisation rate ranging between 50%-60% are expected to have reached at least 85%. These are JMH (55%), Nimule (50%), Ezo (52%), Mapourdit (50%), and Wau (55%). For Jul-Dec 2024 semester, an additional 8 facilities with current utilisation ranging for 20% -39% are expected to have attained at least 85% rate. These are Yei (39%), Munuki (35%), Torit (35%), Makupandu(30%), Rumbek (25%) Kapoeta (27%), Marid (22%) and Gentil (20%). For Jan-June 2025 semester all the remaining 16 facilities whose utilisation rate is below 20%, are expected to reach at least 85%, and this will continue up to the end of GC7. The increased in the unitisation and functionality of GeneXpert machine is expected to positively impact on the EID and VL indicators.</narrative>
    </description>
